25,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are losing our internal experts, and the last time we had trainers visit, the depot supervisors just ignored them.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Our yard hardware is a mess of old models, and trying to switch systems during peak season is a disaster.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The board ignores operating costs but cuts capital. Also, separate licenses for software tend to get more expensive every year.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Last winter, nobody took responsibility for the outage. Plus, our warehouse rules change too fast for any frozen project plan.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"We have a habit of skipping upgrades because we can't test them, and external data migrations have left us with errors for years.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, if nobody is in charge during a crash, that's a huge risk for the few staff I have left.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if we can't even test the dispatch tool, how are we going to handle a whole new ERP?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, the fact that the board approves operating lines easily suggests we should avoid high recurring costs.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Misaki, exactly. We need a clear owner. @Toshio, that's interesting; maybe a fixed-price or bundled approach is better?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, it means we need something that doesn't require a massive, all-at-once testing window.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, does the yard equipment issue mean we need a vendor who actually comes on-site?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"Yes, Misaki. If it doesn't work with the old scanners, the depot floor will just use spreadsheets again.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Toshio,,I am concerned that any modular system with separate add-ons will bleed us dry over time.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Yumi,,We also can't afford a system that is too rigid to change when new accounts arrive.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"And we must avoid external firms that just ""lift"" the data and leave us to fix the route codes.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
