50,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"The candidates are A: Corvus, B: Meridian, C: Tessera, and D: Anchor. I lean toward D because they have engineers on-site.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Kenji,,D sounds best for the yards. B's fixed configuration might be too rigid for our peak-season chaos.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"A is modular, which I fear means rising costs. B is a hosted suite with fixed pricing, which is safer.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"C uses a partner for training, but Misaki said trainers are ignored. B has a regional service team, which is better.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"C's partner-led migration reminds me of the 2018 disaster. D's on-premise approach avoids the ""aging in place"" if they are on-site.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, would B's fixed configuration be too hard for the supervisors to adopt?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, do you think D's on-site team can actually handle the old yard devices?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, if B is a hosted suite, does it avoid the separate license creep I saw in the invoices?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"It should, Toshio. It's a suite, not a collection of separate modules like Corvus.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, an engineering team present through rollout is the only way to ensure the hardware actually works.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm voting for D. We need that hands-on support for the crews.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm with Misaki. D is the only one that feels like it survives the depot floor.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"B is fiscally safer, but if D is on our own servers, the maintenance is more predictable. I can support D.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"If D provides the ownership and stability we lacked last winter, I'm in. I vote D.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,D avoids the external migration risks of C and the modular cost traps of A. I vote D.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
